# ID: GCI-SPL-NET-001
# Title: Rare network destinations across CIM traffic
# Platform: Splunk Enterprise / Splunk Enterprise Security
# Type: Network threat-hunting query
# Data source: Network_Traffic CIM data model
# Required fields: All_Traffic.src, All_Traffic.dest, All_Traffic.dest_port
# Maturity: Draft
# Assumptions: Network_Traffic data model is accelerated and CIM-normalized; use tstats-compatible field names.
# False positives: New SaaS services, CDNs, software updates, scanners and business partner connectivity.
# Tuning: Establish a 14–30 day baseline, exclude approved destinations and tune minimum event/source thresholds by environment.
# ATT&CK: No technique assigned; destination rarity alone is not a behaviour or technique.
# Validation: Not run against a Splunk instance. Confirm data model acceleration and CIM compliance.

| tstats summariesonly=t count AS events dc(All_Traffic.src) AS unique_sources
  FROM datamodel=Network_Traffic.All_Traffic
  WHERE earliest=-24h
  BY All_Traffic.dest All_Traffic.dest_port
| rename All_Traffic.dest AS destination All_Traffic.dest_port AS destination_port
| where events >= 10 AND unique_sources <= 3
| sort - events
